      "content": "thanks, these are great points. i'm also getting some pushback from some older-school economists who say things like \"it'll cause massive inflation\" or \"it'll just make people lazy and stop working.\" it feels like they're just stuck in the past though. do you think those arguments actually hold up against the reality of what AI is doing to the workforce, or are they just outdated talking points?",
